infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title .parse vs .safeParse: fail loud or narrow and render
  desc Same runtime check on the same bytes — opposite behavior at the boundary
  compares
    - label .parse — throws on failure
      children
        - label On success: returns the value typed User directly
        - label On failure: throws a ZodError (paths + messages)
        - label Use where a bad value is a bug to surface
        - label Fail-loud boundary: a server route validating its own DB read
    - label .safeParse — returns a result you narrow
      children
        - label Returns { success: true; data } | { success: false; error }
        - label Narrow on result.success before reaching data or error
        - label Use where a bad value is an expected outcome
        - label Render it: form input, third-party webhook
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
